-- title:
--   Lemma 13 — physical recording law
-- statement:
--   Throughout, the rewards are rounded, the identification array is arbitrary and fixed first, and probabilities are over the fresh-row law: independent complete rows, private tapes, and $J$ read from the coordinator's tape. On every enabled round the recorded arm of p.28 satisfies (9): $\Pr(I_t=i\mid\mathcal F_t)=\xi_i$ and $\Pr(I_t=\bot\mid\mathcal F_t)=1-\sum_i\xi_i$. On $I_t=j$, the owner's observation is $r_t(j)$, so its increment is the one specified by (10).
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: the fresh-row execution → the fresh-row reference execution on the construction branch; reason: Section 5 and Lemma 19 work with the reference execution, and p.20 fixes it for Sections 4-6
--   - encoding: the pre-round history F_t → `preRound`, a filtration on the fresh-row space; reason: the physical part of the history of p.14, generated by exposed coordinates
-- source:
--   Gan, Square-Root Regret for Adversarial Multiplayer Bandits without Collision Information or Shared Randomness, arXiv:2610.05688, Lemma 13, p.28

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AdvMultiplayer_FreshRow

open MeasureTheory

namespace AdvMultiplayer

/-- **Lemma 13 (physical recording law).** Gan, arXiv:2610.05688, Lemma 13, p.28. In the fresh-row
execution, on every enabled round, `I_t` satisfies (9):
`Pr(I_t = i | ℱ_t) = ξ_i`, `Pr(I_t = ⊥ | ℱ_t) = 1 - Σ_i ξ_i`. On `I_t = j` the owner's observation is
`r_t(j)`, so its increment is the one specified by (10).

**Formalization Note.** `recAt` also names the source, the owner of the played arm. The rates `ξ` are
the coordinator's registers, which are the episode's frozen rates. -/
theorem lemma_13 (p : Size) (hb : p.branch) (idA : IdArray p) (r : Rewards p) (hr : IsRounded p r) :
    (∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 p.T, ∀ j : Fin p.K, ∀ᵐ x ∂(freshLaw p),
      enabledAt p (freshTrace p idA r x) t →
      ((freshLaw p)[Set.indicator {x | ∃ i, recAt p (idA, x.1) (freshTrace p idA r x) t = some (i, j)}
          (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) | (preRound p) t]) x =
        (coAt p (freshTrace p idA r x) t).co.xi (j.val + 1)) ∧
    (∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 p.T, ∀ᵐ x ∂(freshLaw p),
      enabledAt p (freshTrace p idA r x) t →
      ((freshLaw p)[Set.indicator {x | recAt p (idA, x.1) (freshTrace p idA r x) t = none}
          (fun _ => (1 : ℝ)) | (preRound p) t]) x =
        1 - ∑ j : Fin p.K, (coAt p (freshTrace p idA r x) t).co.xi (j.val + 1)) ∧
    ∀ᵐ x ∂(freshLaw p), ∀ t ∈ Finset.Icc 1 p.T, ∀ i j,
      recAt p (idA, x.1) (freshTrace p idA r x) t = some (i, j) →
      (freshTrace p idA r x t).obs (playerOf p i) = r t j ∧
      calArrival p (idA, x.1) (freshTrace p idA r x) t j =
        arrivalOf p p.eta ((coAt p (freshTrace p idA r x) t).co.xi (j.val + 1)) (r t j) := by sorry

end AdvMultiplayer
